Z||000000||fierocd||08-30-2001||09:40 PM||||OK, first of, I have an 86 GT, 4 speed.  I just got it running great!  It has ton of power but has one problem, every time it warms up, it dies whenever I go to stop or push in the clutch.  It desn't even try to idle, the RPM's just go straight down to 0.<BR>New parts include coil, cap, rotor, ignition module, pick-up coil, plugs, wires, fuel pump, fuel pressure regulator, timing chain and gears, oil pump, lifters and pushrods, fuel filter (2-3 months ago), PCV valve, MAP sensor, clutch, oil pressure sending unit. and some others that I can't remember.<BR>The fuel pump is new from Auto Zone but I can hear it humming all the time.  The oil pressure at idle sits just below 40.  The temp is between 160 and 220.  When cold, the idle is about 1100-1200 then goes down to 1000-900.  Timing is at 10.  Any ideas on what to check||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierocd||08-30-2001||10:24 PM||||Forgot one thing, the only trouble code is 24, speed sensor.  The wires are cut for some reason and I haven't fixed it yet.||||reg||1
