Z||000003||PBJ||08-30-2001||10:49 PM||||I would suggest you start by removing the IAC motor/valve and attempt to move it in or out an 1/8 of an inch to see if it is siezed-this device controls engine idle.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forsalestart.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierocd||08-30-2001||10:56 PM||||What about the fuel pump humming all the time?  It did this before, but only when I had less than a 1/4 tank left.  Then the pump sounded really bad so I replaced it.  Now I can hear it humming all the time.  Is that normal?  It doesn't sound really loud but it is enough that I can hear it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||PBJ||08-30-2001||10:59 PM||||It is normal to hear the fuel pump (when you are listening for it).  Also if you installed it and it is now touching the bottem or side or bafle within the tank it will make a louder sound.  IF you are concerned about the fuel pump check the pressure to be sure.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forsalestart.jpg"> ||||reg||1
